# Edit path to your clone. Crontab format: minute hour day month weekday
#
# Logging uses shell redirect (>> file), not Python. The shell cannot create
# logs/ by itself — use mkdir -p logs BEFORE ./scripts/run_pipeline.sh in the
# same line so the redirect can open logs/pipeline.log.
#
# Run daily at 06:15 (server local time):
# 15 6 * * * cd /absolute/path/to/basic-etl-pipeline && mkdir -p logs && ./scripts/run_pipeline.sh >> /absolute/path/to/basic-etl-pipeline/logs/pipeline.log 2>&1
#
# (run_pipeline.sh also runs mkdir -p logs at startup, but that runs too late for
# the redirect above — the mkdir in THIS line is what matters for cron.)
